# Responsive Design (Mobile + Desktop)

This is a public marketing/e-commerce site — a large share of traffic will be mobile.
Every component or page must work well at both ends of the viewport range, not just desktop.

## Rules

- **Mobile-first**: unprefixed Tailwind classes = the mobile layout, then layer
  `sm:` / `md:` / `lg:` for larger screens.
- **Grids/multi-column layouts must collapse on mobile.** Never ship a bare
  `grid-cols-3`; write `grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3`.
- **Horizontal nav bars / link lists with 3+ items need a real mobile pattern**
  (e.g. a hamburger/drawer menu) — shrinking font size or padding until it
  barely fits is not acceptable.
- **Avoid fixed pixel widths** (`w-[600px]`) on containers that should reflow;
  prefer `max-w-*` + `w-full`.
- **Reuse the fluid `clamp()`-based tokens** already defined in
  `app/globals.css` (`--section-y`, `--gutter`, `--nav-h`, etc.) instead of a
  single hardcoded font-size/padding value.
- **Touch targets** (buttons, links) should be at least ~44px tall on mobile.
- **Test every new section at two widths** before considering it done: ~375px
  (mobile) and ~1440px (desktop) — use the browser tool's device emulation.

## Example

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — breaks below ~900px, text/columns get squeezed
<div className="grid grid-cols-3 gap-6">

// ✅ GOOD — mobile-first, expands at the md breakpoint
<div className="grid grid-cols-1 gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
```
